        "id": "ch06.s13.p01",
        "sentences": [
          {
            "id": "ch06.s13.p01.r01",
            "text": "How can a local model be turned into an automatic evaluator for instruction-following outputs, and why is that useful here?",
            "type": "C",
            "cites": []
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s13.p01.r02",
            "text": "Ollama is software, or an application, for efficiently running large language models on a laptop.",
            "type": "F",
            "cites": [
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@1475",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@1479",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@1496",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@1498",
              "7m2jV7BOFkA@1500"
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "ch06.s13.p01.r03",
            "text": "It lets you run local models such as Llama 3, Mistral, and Gemma 2 on a PC or laptop.",
